#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>AddXid()</0> registers <1>XidClient</1> as a singleton and wires <2>IHttpClientFactory</2> for JWKS fetching."
msgstr "<0>AddXid()</0> registers <1>XidClient</1> as a singleton and wires <2>IHttpClientFactory</2> for JWKS fetching."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>Claims</0> embeds <1>jwt.RegisteredClaims</1> and adds <2>ClientID</2>, <3>Scope</3>, <4>AMR</4>, <5>ACR</5>, <6>OrgID</6>, <7>OrgSlug</7>."
msgstr "<0>Claims</0> embeds <1>jwt.RegisteredClaims</1> and adds <2>ClientID</2>, <3>Scope</3>, <4>AMR</4>, <5>ACR</5>, <6>OrgID</6>, <7>OrgSlug</7>."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>createXidServerMiddleware</0> returns an H3 handler that verifies a Bearer or explicit application JWT and writes <1>event.context.xidAuth</1>. Configure same-origin Core sessions through <2>sessionTokenExchange</2>; H3 v1 relative URLs also require a trusted <3>requestOrigin</3>. Place the file in <4>server/middleware/</4> for global Nitro registration."
msgstr "<0>createXidServerMiddleware</0> returns an H3 handler that verifies a Bearer or explicit application JWT and writes <1>event.context.xidAuth</1>. Configure same-origin Core sessions through <2>sessionTokenExchange</2>; H3 v1 relative URLs also require a trusted <3>requestOrigin</3>. Place the file in <4>server/middleware/</4> for global Nitro registration."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>event.context.xidAuth</0> is server-side only and is never sent to the browser."
msgstr "<0>event.context.xidAuth</0> is server-side only and is never sent to the browser."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>false</0> deprovisions the user and revokes active sessions."
msgstr "<0>false</0> deprovisions the user and revokes active sessions."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>GET /auth/config</0> returns the public Hosted Auth configuration for the organization. Provider secrets and disabled providers are not returned to the browser."
msgstr "<0>GET /auth/config</0> returns the public Hosted Auth configuration for the organization. Provider secrets and disabled providers are not returned to the browser."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>getAuth</0> verifies a Bearer token, explicit application JWT cookie, optional same-origin Core exchange, or the configured Remix session JWT, then returns an <1>AuthResult</1>. <2>requireAuth</2> throws a 302 redirect to <3>redirectPath</3> when unauthenticated."
msgstr "<0>getAuth</0> verifies a Bearer token, explicit application JWT cookie, optional same-origin Core exchange, or the configured Remix session JWT, then returns an <1>AuthResult</1>. <2>requireAuth</2> throws a 302 redirect to <3>redirectPath</3> when unauthenticated."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>getToken()</0> returns a short-lived JWT (60 s) cached only in memory by <1>TokenManager</1> in <2>@xid-kit/core</2>."
msgstr "<0>getToken()</0> returns a short-lived JWT (60 s) cached only in memory by <1>TokenManager</1> in <2>@xid-kit/core</2>."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>getToken()</0> returns a short-lived JWT for API calls. Verify networklessly on your backend with JWKS."
msgstr "<0>getToken()</0> returns a short-lived JWT for API calls. Verify networklessly on your backend with JWKS."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>handleCallback</0> validates the <1>state</1> parameter against the session to prevent CSRF."
msgstr "<0>handleCallback</0> validates the <1>state</1> parameter against the session to prevent CSRF."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>handleCallback</0> validates the <1>state</1> parameter to prevent CSRF, exchanges the authorization code, and returns a <2>Response</2> with <3>Set-Cookie</3>."
msgstr "<0>handleCallback</0> validates the <1>state</1> parameter to prevent CSRF, exchanges the authorization code, and returns a <2>Response</2> with <3>Set-Cookie</3>."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>jwtKey</0> is a JWKS public key; it is safe for networkless verification and does not contain a private key."
msgstr "<0>jwtKey</0> is a JWKS public key; it is safe for networkless verification and does not contain a private key."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>load()</0> reads <1>/v1/me</1> and hydrates user, session, and active organization."
msgstr "<0>load()</0> reads <1>/v1/me</1> and hydrates user, session, and active organization."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>POST /scim/v2/organizations/{organization_id}/Bulk</0> accepts a <1>BulkRequest</1> with up to 100 operations and a 1 MiB payload limit. Responses return per-operation HTTP status in a <2>BulkResponse</2> even when some operations fail."
msgstr "<0>POST /scim/v2/organizations/{organization_id}/Bulk</0> accepts a <1>BulkRequest</1> with up to 100 operations and a 1 MiB payload limit. Responses return per-operation HTTP status in a <2>BulkResponse</2> even when some operations fail."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>secretKey</0> (<1>sk_live_xxx</1>) must stay server-side only; never pass it to an island or client bundle."
msgstr "<0>secretKey</0> (<1>sk_live_xxx</1>) must stay server-side only; never pass it to an island or client bundle."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>ServiceProviderConfig</0> advertises <1>sort.supported=true</1>, <2>bulk.supported=true</2>, and <3>etag.supported=true</3>."
msgstr "<0>ServiceProviderConfig</0> advertises <1>sort.supported=true</1>, <2>bulk.supported=true</2>, and <3>etag.supported=true</3>."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>setActiveOrganization()</0> switches org context and clears the token cache before reloading state."
msgstr "<0>setActiveOrganization()</0> switches org context and clears the token cache before reloading state."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>signIn()</0> builds the PKCE S256 authorize URL, stores the verifier, OAuth state, and nonce in the token cache, opens the browser adapter, and exchanges the returned code for a verified native session. Browser failure, state mismatch, ID token verification, and token exchange errors surface as <1>signInState.status === 'error'</1>."
msgstr "<0>signIn()</0> builds the PKCE S256 authorize URL, stores the verifier, OAuth state, and nonce in the token cache, opens the browser adapter, and exchanges the returned code for a verified native session. Browser failure, state mismatch, ID token verification, and token exchange errors surface as <1>signInState.status === 'error'</1>."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>signInPassword()</0> establishes a cookie session through Hosted Auth password flow."
msgstr "<0>signInPassword()</0> establishes a cookie session through Hosted Auth password flow."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>signOut()</0> revokes the browser session cookie."
msgstr "<0>signOut()</0> revokes the browser session cookie."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>urn:xid:aal3</0> is not currently issued. WebAuthn UV and BE/BS flags do not prove the non-exportable hardware key required by NIST; AAL3 requests fail explicitly and the current maximum mapping is AAL2."
msgstr "<0>urn:xid:aal3</0> is not currently issued. WebAuthn UV and BE/BS flags do not prove the non-exportable hardware key required by NIST; AAL3 requests fail explicitly and the current maximum mapping is AAL2."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>useAuth().isSignedIn</0> reflects the locally stored, verified native session from <1>XidProvider</1>. It does not read a web cookie session; offline_access is rejected until DPoP sender binding is implemented, and access-token expiry requires reauthorization."
msgstr "<0>useAuth().isSignedIn</0> reflects the locally stored, verified native session from <1>XidProvider</1>. It does not read a web cookie session; offline_access is rejected until DPoP sender binding is implemented, and access-token expiry requires reauthorization."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>Xid.authenticate_request</0> accepts both a Rack env hash and a Rack <1>Request</1> object."
msgstr "<0>Xid.authenticate_request</0> accepts both a Rack env hash and a Rack <1>Request</1> object."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>XidError</0> uses <1>thiserror</1> for structured error variants including <2>JwtValidation</2>, <3>JwksFetch</3>, <4>KeyNotFound</4>, <5>IssuerMismatch</5>, and webhook-specific variants."
msgstr "<0>XidError</0> uses <1>thiserror</1> for structured error variants including <2>JwtValidation</2>, <3>JwksFetch</3>, <4>KeyNotFound</4>, <5>IssuerMismatch</5>, and webhook-specific variants."

#: apps/site/src/content-source/docs/message-descriptors.ts
msgid "<0>xidMiddleware()</0> verifies a Bearer or explicit application JWT on the Edge Runtime. For a same-origin Core session, it exchanges the opaque cookie through <1>/v1/sessions/token</1>, verifies the returned JWT, and injects auth state into downstream server request headers."
msgstr "<0>xidMiddleware()</0> verifies a Bearer or explicit application JWT on the Edge Runtime. For a same-origin Core session, it exchanges the opaque cookie through <1>/v1/sessions/token</1>, verifies the returned JWT, and injects auth state into downstream server request headers."

